1
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:19,333
The imagination behind Wuthering Heights.

2
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:32,666
Emily is a history, drama, romance film directed by Frances O'Connor.

3
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
The imagined life of one of the world’s most famous authors, Emily Brontë, as she
finds her voice and writes the literary classic Wuthering Heights.

4
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
Explore the relationships that inspired her – her raw, passionate sisterhood with Charlotte and Anne; her first
aching, forbidden love for Weightman and her care for her maverick brother whom she idolises.

5
00:36:06,666 --> 00:36:12,666
Emily Brontë, played by Emma Mackey.

6
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Branwell Brontë, played by Fionn Whitehead.

7
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
William Weightman, played by Oliver Jackson-Cohen.

8
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Charlotte Brontë, played by Alexandra Dowling.

9
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Aunt Branwell, played by Gemma Jones.

10
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
Patrick Brontë, played by Adrian Dunbar.

11
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
Emily is a 2022 British biographical drama film written and
directed by Frances O'Connor in her directorial debut.

12
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It is a part-fictional portrait of English writer Emily Brontë (played by Emma Mackey),
concentrating on a fictional romantic relationship with the young curate William Weightman.

13
01:33:53,333 --> 01:33:59,333
Fionn Whitehead, Oliver Jackson-Cohen, Alexandra Dowling, Amelia Gething,
Adrian Dunbar and Gemma Jones appear in supporting roles.

14
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
Emily premiered at the 2022 Toronto International Film Festival before being
theatrically released in the United Kingdom by Warner Bros.

15
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:26,000
Pictures on 14 October 2022.

16
01:55:33,333 --> 01:55:39,333
The film explores themes of england, author, woman
director, deathbed, fictional biography.

17
02:02:46,666 --> 02:02:52,666
The tone is emotional.
